{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.LocalQZetaFunction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.LocalQZetaFunction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.Polynomial.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Complex.Analytic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent"],"declarations":16,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.weil_partner_complex_witness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.weil_partner_complex_witness","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/LocalQZetaFunction.lean#L134-L140","doc":"The complex witness: `q = 4`, `α = 2i`, partner `= −2i = conj α`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.weil_partner_real_witness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.weil_partner_real_witness","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/LocalQZetaFunction.lean#L129-L132","doc":"The real (supersingular) witness: `q = 4`, `α = 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.weil_partner_eq_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.weil_partner_eq_conj","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/LocalQZetaFunction.lean#L106-L118","doc":"**The functional-equation partner is the complex conjugate.** For a nonzero\n`α` with `‖α‖² = q`, the partner `q/α` supplied by the functional equation\nequals `conj α`.\n\nThis is what makes `|α| = √q` a *symmetry* statement rather than a bare\nmagnitude bound: the eigenvalue multiset is closed under conjugation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.LocalQZetaFunction.charPoly_roots","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.LocalQZetaFunction.charPoly_roots","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/LocalQZetaFunction.lean#L95-L95","doc":"`P̃` factors as `∏ᵢ (X − αᵢ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.LocalQZetaFunction.charPoly_degree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.LocalQZetaFunction.charPoly_degree","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/LocalQZetaFunction.lean#L93-L93","doc":"`P̃` has degree `2g = 8`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.LocalQZetaFunction.charPoly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.LocalQZetaFunction.charPoly","kind":"def","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/LocalQZetaFunction.lean#L91-L91","doc":"The *reversed* characteristic polynomial `P̃(X) = ∏ᵢ (X − αᵢ)`.\nRelated to the standard form `P(t) = ∏ᵢ (1 − αᵢ t)` by\n`P(t) = t^{2g} · P̃(1/t)`, so the roots of `P̃` are the eigenvalues\n`αᵢ` themselves (not their reciprocals). We use this convention\nto match Lean's polynomial root factorization. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.LocalQZetaFunction.eigenvalues_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.LocalQZetaFunction.eigenvalues_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/LocalQZetaFunction.lean#L85-L85","doc":"No eigenvalue vanishes.\n\nFrobenius acts invertibly on `H¹`, with `det(Fr_q) = ±q^g ≠ 0`, so no\nroot of the characteristic polynomial is zero. It does not follow from\n`charPoly_roots`, which permits zero roots, so it is carried as a field.\n\nAdded 2026-08-28. Without it `eigenvalue_norm_sq_axiom` in\n`hasse-weil-bound.lean` is not merely unproved but FALSE: the all-zeros\ndatum satisfies every other field and every hypothesis of that axiom, and\nits conclusion `‖αᵢ‖² = q` then reads `0 = q`, contradicting `q_pos`.\nMachine-checked before the axiom was replaced by a proof. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.LocalQZetaFunction.eigenvalues","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.LocalQZetaFunction.eigenvalues","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/LocalQZetaFunction.lean#L73-L73","doc":"The 8 fundamental Frobenius eigenvalues `α₁, …, α₈`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.LocalQZetaFunction.q_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.LocalQZetaFunction.q_pos","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/LocalQZetaFunction.lean#L71-L71","doc":"The base field has more than one element, so `q > 0`.\n\nRestored 2026-08-28. The pre-migration structure carried this field\ncommented out, annotated `-- (archimedean; not meaningful over R_q)` --\nan author wanting exactly this hypothesis and unable to state it, which\nis independent evidence for the `q : ℝ` correction above. Its absence is\nwhy `hasse_weil_bound` referenced a nonexistent `Z.q_pos`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.LocalQZetaFunction.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.LocalQZetaFunction.q","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/LocalQZetaFunction.lean#L63-L63","doc":"The cardinality of the base field, as a real number.\n\n**Corrected 2026-08-28 (bean `qou-lsib`).** This field was `q : R_q`,\ni.e. a formal Laurent polynomial over `ℤ`. That contradicted both its own\nnarrative and every other field of this structure. The `.md` defines the\nobject as the classical Weil zeta function of Bring's curve over a finite\nfield — it counts `|ℬ(𝔽_{q^n})|`, its polynomial is the characteristic\npolynomial of `Fr_q`, and the Hasse-Weil bound it exists to state is\n`|αᵢ| = √q` — while `eigenvalues` and `charPoly` were already `ℂ`-valued.\nA field size is not a formal parameter, and `√q`, `q^ρ` and `|α|² ≤ q` are\nnot statements about `ℤ[q, q⁻¹]`: `R_q` carries no order and no norm, so\nthe two downstream results were not merely unproved but unstatable.\n\nThis is the archimedean side of the wall (§7c): the ordering and `rpow`\nthe consumers need are exactly the constructs that require `ℝ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.LocalQZetaFunction.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.LocalQZetaFunction.mk","kind":"ctor","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/LocalQZetaFunction.lean#L47-L47","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.LocalQZetaFunction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.LocalQZetaFunction","kind":"structure","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/LocalQZetaFunction.lean#L38-L96","doc":"**Local q-zeta function** of Bring's curve.\n\nEncodes the generating function for point counts over finite\nextensions of `F_q`. The characteristic polynomial `P(t)` has degree\n`2g = 8`, with roots `α₁, …, α₈` — the fundamental Frobenius\neigenvalues.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:local-q-zeta-function}`\nRef: [leitner2026] Chapter 8, Section 4 ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:local-q-zeta-function","label":"def:local-q-zeta-function","md":"quantum-observable-universe/q-geometric-langlands/local-q-zeta-function.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.bringsGenus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.bringsGenus","kind":"def","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/LocalQZetaFunction.lean#L35-L36","doc":"The genus of Bring's curve. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.q_inv_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.q_inv_param","kind":"def","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/LocalQZetaFunction.lean#L32-L33","doc":"The formal parameter `q⁻¹` of the ground ring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.q_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.q_param","kind":"def","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/LocalQZetaFunction.lean#L29-L30","doc":"The formal parameter `q` of the ground ring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.R_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.R_q","kind":"def","line":26,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/LocalQZetaFunction.lean#L26-L27","doc":"Ground ring `R_q = ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` (Laurent polynomials over `ℤ`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}